{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Hamiltonian path, or nil when there is none (or no vertex): the first one a depth-first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"backtracking search finds, from each vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, extending through each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FindHamiltonianPath"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"hamiltonianPath","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Path","identifier":"doc:\/\/Walks\/documentation\/Walks\/Path","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks4PathV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"name":"Complexity","type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exponential in the worst case (n! paths); O(degree) per step of the search,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"plus O(n + m) for the reachability test where it can fail (not after a step from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex with no other unvisited successor, so a path or cycle graph takes O(n + m))."}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/hamiltonianpath()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/hamiltonianPath()"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph"]]},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Hamiltonian.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/Hamiltonian.swift#L517"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5ToursE15hamiltonianPath5Walks0F0Vy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgyF","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"Tours","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"title":"hamiltonianPath()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"hamiltonianPath"},{"text":"() -> ","